From: Gopi Chandra Sekhar Reddy Kanala <gopi.kanala@oss.qualcomm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: qcom: lpass-lpi: Force runtime suspend on system sleep

The LPASS LPI pin controller votes for the LPASS HW_MACRO and HW_DCODEC
clocks through pm_clk and only implements runtime PM callbacks. Its
consumers, such as the SoundWire controllers, keep it runtime active
through their device links. If a consumer is active when system suspend
starts, or is resumed during it, the runtime PM usage count the PM core
holds from the prepare phase keeps the pin controller from runtime
suspending, and both clock votes are held for the whole suspend. On
Glymur CRD this keeps CX and DDR from collapsing in s2idle.

Use pm_runtime_force_suspend() and pm_runtime_force_resume() as the
system sleep callbacks so the clocks are always released at system
suspend. Consumers are suspended before their suppliers, so the pin
controller goes down after them and comes back before them.

[ retroforge: posted for pinctrl-sm8650-lpass-lpi.c only, v1
  <20261112-lpass-lpi-system-sleep-v1-1-438cb997e0e9@oss.qualcomm.com>;
  the same line is added here to all twelve LPI drivers, which the
  thread agrees have the same problem (v2 is to move the dev_pm_ops into
  pinctrl-lpass-lpi.c). Found independently on SM8550 before the posting
  was seen.

  HW 2026-11-14, AYANEO Pocket ACE (SM8550), 7.3.4, 25 s suspends, the
  suspend engine closing the playback stream about 2 s before the kernel
  suspends (inside the 3 s SoundWire autosuspend), sensors PD not
  attached: without this, time in aosd/cxsd in the first suspend after
  boot only (0 of 12 after it, ddr in all); with it, in 15 of 15 (19.5
  to 21.8 s in 14, 8.8 s in the first after boot). Playback back after
  every resume. Traced: on the forced system-sleep path neither vote was
  released, on a runtime suspend of the audio chain both were. Only the
  SM8550 driver is HW-tested here. ]
---
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-milos-lpass-lpi.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-milos-lpass-lpi.c
@@ -246,6 +246,7 @@
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, lpi_pinctrl_of_match);
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops lpi_pinctrl_pm_ops = {
+	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(pm_clk_suspend, pm_clk_resume, NULL)
 };
 
